ees to make post-baccalaureate education as accessible and exciting as possible. For more information, fill out our inquiry form or apply today!\nVisit the ISU Graduate School in the Museum Building, room 401, in Pocatello, ID, or email us at gradschool@isu.edu, or give us a call at 208-282-2150.\nWhat's Happening, Grad Bengals?\nCongratulations to our 3MT winners and all participants! Your presentations and the work you are doing as graduate students here at ISU impressed us as always!\n\ud83e\udd47First Place: Will Kimball, Chemistry - MS\n\ud83e\udd48Second Place: Katelyn Cathcart, Clinical Psychology - PhD\n\ud83e\udd49Third Place: Michelle Collier, Public Administration - MPA\n\ud83c\udfc5People's Choice: Brenda Phillips, Occupational Therapy - MOT\nLearn more about the amazing stories of ISU Grad Bengals by checking out the Graduate School blog! Want to be featured? Fill out the student feature form, and we'll reach out to you!\nGraduate School News\nEncourage Graduate Students to Participate in the Three Minute Thesis Competition\nCall for Judges, Moderators, and Volunteers for the 2026 Research and Creative Works Symposium\nIdaho Statewide 3MT\u00ae Competition Feb 17\nAll Graduate News >>\nWhat Can You Do With a Graduate Degree?\nBecome Educators and Leaders in Your Field\nExpand Your Passion: Gain Specific and Hands-On Experience\nIncrease Your Earning Potential\nContact Us\ngradschool@isu.edu\n(208) 282-2150\nIdaho State University921 S. 8th Ave, Mail Stop 8075Pocatello, ID 83209-8075\nGraduate School Team\nHow Can We Help You?\nApply Now\nRequest Information\nGraduate Catalog\nTuition Information\nTheses & Dissertations\nSubmit to the Graduate Weekly\nFacebook Feed\nColleges and Schools\nBusiness\nGraduate School\nHumanities, Education, and Social Sciences\nNursing, Rehabilitation, and Human Health\nSchool of the Arts\nPharmacy and Health Professions\nScience and Engineering\nTechnology\nResources\nAccessibility\nA-Z Index\nBookstore\nCampus Map\nCanvas\